\n\nThe past year I have kind lost interest in the UB as my 250 KTM just feels so much more comfortable over rough terrain, but I don't love the 240+ lbs weight of the thing.\nIt's apparent that all these e-bikes with a 53\" - ish wheelbase are simply too short except for smooth terrain, they are a scalpel & tons of fun in those conditions.\u00a0 \n\nIf fitting this swingarm - are there any other issues needing resolved like brake lines, jackshaft mods & such ? \nDo the stock linkage components fit up properly ? \nIt's a given that a new longer chain would be in order, so thats expected. \nGuess a new swingarm would be excuse enough for finally taking apart & servicing the jackshaft arrangement .. not looking forward to that battle. \nThanks for the content, carry on.","likes":0,"publishedAt":"2026-08-01T01:34:07Z","videoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TXw1CtY2yQg","awaitingReply":false},{"id":"Ugz2ZyM52Z9_JtsCXEx4AaABAg","author":"@jimji2774","avatar":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","text":"Very interesting. One more rather expensive upgrade for the Surron but on the other hand all this stuff is mainly available only for Surron so its a double edged sword. Sure makes me want this part thanks.","likes":0,"publishedAt":"2026-07-24T23:45:03Z","videoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TXw1CtY2yQg","awaitingReply":false},{"id":"UgwRJraNipJk0gtfuYJ4AaABAg","author":"@jimji2774","avatar":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","text":"Nice video review but that is some real open riding and not a tree in sight lol. Would be nice to do some more testing in tighter technical terrain -and another expensive aftermarket part to try and improve a Chinese emoto. When is Dust and Bonnell ever going to release theirs bikes that might have all these things done from the factory or at least be closer to a the best gas bikes. Thanks for taking the time.","likes":0,"publishedAt":"2026-07-24T17:52:19Z","videoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bCUglq5XaKw","awaitingReply":false}],"hasNewComments"